                <pb facs="0674" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4392: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-03T12:00:00-05:45">April 3,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>83. Department’s 46, April 2, 1 p.m. Brigade commander reports that there has
                    been absolutely no friction along the frontier. He states that majority of
                    followers of Salgado and Ortez are Hondurans and when hard pressed by marines
                    these men cross into Honduras and their many friends there immediately report to
                    Tegucigalpa that marines have invaded Honduras. He reports that General Mendoza
                    is the only Honduran leader who is cooperating with marines.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
